<!--
    kuna issue testcase: code whose address the program takes, and that no flow
    reaches, is a function entry (`option addrtakenentry on|off`, default-ON).

    Issue:      kuna GH-1039 sections 1 and 2 - a handler called only through a
                pointer that a `lea` stores is missing from the inventory and
                folded into the function before it, and so are handlers a
                relocated table names before the first RUNTIME_FUNCTION.
    Stage:      P1 code/data partition - the Listing walk's committed function
                set (`aif/kuna_addrtakenentry.rs`, re-seeding the walk behind
                `fast_funcdisc` and `funcdisc_recursive`).
    P0 assert:  `option addrtakenentry on|off`.

    The XML wrapper only provides the harness architecture.  Every pass clears
    it and loads `pe_addrtaken_x86_64.exe` (source `pe_addrtaken_x86_64.py`
    beside it).  `.pdata` describes only _start (0x140001052), which calls
    register (0x140001030).  register stores `lea rax,[0x140001040]` to a
    global and _start calls the handler through it; pre_a (0x140001000) and
    pre_b (0x140001010) are named only by relocated words in `.rdata`, before
    the first record.  The look-alikes are not functions: a UTF-16 string at
    0x140001020 (relocated and lea'd), `runon` at 0x140001050 (lea'd, falls
    into _start), the interior address 0x140001043, a data blob shaped like a
    MinGW delay-import descriptor at 0x1400010a0 (lea'd after a ret, decodes
    to add [rax],eax ; add [rax],al ; ... ; ret 0), the computed-goto return
    block 0x1400010c0 (add rsp,0x28 ; ret) that interp (0x1400010b0) takes
    with lea and reaches with `jmp rax`, a relocated stub past the last record at 0x1400010d0 and a
    lea'd string at 0x1400010e0.

    Pass 1 (`mode fast`, `option addrtakenentry off`) reproduces the bug: only
    _start, register and interp.
    Pass 2 (`mode fast`, shipped default) adds pre_a, pre_b and the handler,
    and the handler decompiles to its own body.
    Passes 3 and 4 repeat that in `mode aggressive`.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
